WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Here is the graph of y
equals x squared plus one.

2
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.310
It floats above the x-axis.

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.880
It never crosses.

4
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:12.630
So x squared equals minus
one has no real solution.

5
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.390
What if we simply define a new number, i,

6
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.770
whose square is minus one?

7
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:18.880
Is that allowed?

8
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.820
Or is it a made-up trick, just cheating?

9
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.700
In this mission, you'll write
complex numbers in Cartesian form,

10
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.240
a plus b i, with a real
part and an imaginary part.

11
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.290
You'll calculate with them:
expand the brackets as usual,

12
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.560
then replace i squared with minus one.

13
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:40.990
And you'll use the quadratic formula
when the discriminant is negative.

14
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.260
Your mission: decide whether inventing
a solution to x squared equals minus one

15
00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:47.570
is just cheating.
